# KDE Plasma 6 Wayland Suite — Cursor CLI Rules

You have access to the `kde-wayland-suite` in this repository.

When the user asks about keyboard layouts (ABNT2, US-intl, cedilla), broken
shortcuts (Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V stopping system-wide), Tongfang/Avell keyboard matrix lock,
smart keyboard power management, touchpad gestures, the Logitech MX Master 3S,
battery/power consumption, or AI host harness alignment in KDE Plasma 6 Wayland:

1. Full diagnostic:
   `./bin/kde-config status` or `make check`
2. Fix keyboard shortcuts and cedilla support (US-intl, Chrome, Orca, Electron, GTK, Qt):
   `./bin/kde-config fix-keyboard` or `make fix-keyboard`
3. Fix Tongfang / Avell / Clevo hardware keyboard matrix (GRUB i8042 / ACPI):
   `./bin/kde-config fix-tongfang` or `make fix-tongfang`
4. Smart Keyboard Power Management (anti-latch + battery saver):
   `./bin/kde-config smart-keyboard-power --apply` or `make smart-keyboard-power`
5. Configure AI Host Harness & Model Role Profile:
   `./bin/kde-config configure-harness`
6. Touchpad gestures (libinput-gestures):
   `./bin/kde-config gestures` or `make gestures`
7. Logitech MX Master 3S (logiops):
   `./bin/kde-config mouse` or `make mouse`
8. Battery/power diagnostic (read-only):
   `./bin/kde-config battery-status` or `make battery-status`
9. Interactive Report & History:
   `./bin/kde-config report` or `./bin/kde-config report --list`
10. Central Help:
   `./bin/kde-config help`
11. Switch active keyboard layout:
   `./bin/kde-config switch br` or `./bin/kde-config switch us`

Never apply a battery fix without asking the user first — `battery-apply` only
acts on the `BATTERY_FIX_*` variables you pass, and each one is opt-in.
`battery-revert` undoes the last application.

Report every command using the standardized 4-phase output format defined in
`base/shared/OUTPUT-CONTRACT.md`: **Plano** → **Execução** → **Resumo** → **Ações Recomendadas**.
It is identical across Claude Code, Cursor, OMP, OpenCode and Antigravity.
